		{
			dependencies: ["308B363D1029D44E"]
			description: [
				"Though feared by most surface dwellers, the mysterious &8Deep Ones&r are not naturally hostile."
				""
				"These ancient inhabitants of the &1Abyssal Chasm&r have long guarded their submerged civilization, watching over the ruins and sacred altars scattered throughout the ocean floor. Those who approach them peacefully may earn their trust—and with it, valuable rewards."
				""
				"Treat them with respect, for every action influences how they perceive you."
				""
				"{image:ftb:textures/alex_caves_pearl_trading_1.png width:200 height:130 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"Throughout the Abyssal Chasm you'll discover &bAbyssal Altars&r, sacred sites where offerings can be presented to the Deep Ones."
				""
				"Place either a &dPearl&r or a &bHeart of the Sea&r upon an altar and wait patiently. Nearby Deep Ones will investigate your offering, and if they accept it, they will leave behind a gift in exchange."
				""
				"Each successful offering increases your reputation with the Deep Ones, gradually strengthening your relationship with their civilization."
				""
				"Attacking Deep Ones, however, will reduce your reputation and make earning their trust far more difficult."
				""
				"{image:ftb:textures/alex_caves_pearl_trading_2.png width:180 height:130 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"You'll know your offering has been accepted when the &bAbyssal Altar&r begins to glow and a reward materializes upon its surface."
				""
				"As your reputation continues to grow, the Deep Ones will become increasingly friendly. Adventurers who earn their complete trust may even find these ancient beings willing to fight alongside them when danger arises."
				""
				"Sometimes, the greatest treasures are earned not through conquest—"
				""
				"—but through diplomacy."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "alexscaves:abyssal_altar"
				tag: { }
