		{
			dependencies: ["172EE8617C59F90A"]
			description: [
				"The &8Forlorn Hollows&r are home to countless creatures that have adapted to survive within its endless darkness."
				""
				"Among the first you'll encounter are the relentless &6Corrodents&r, the elusive &5Gloomoths&r, and the fanatical &8Underzealots&r. Though vastly different in appearance and behavior, each plays an important role within the fragile ecosystem of this forgotten world."
				""
				"Learning to survive among them is the first step toward mastering the Hollows."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"Few creatures are as common—or as troublesome—as the &6Corrodent&r."
				""
				"These oversized scavengers burrow through ancient ruins and feast upon anything left behind by the civilizations that once called this place home. Their powerful teeth are even capable of chewing through &8Guanostone&r, allowing them to carve tunnels and nests throughout the cavern walls."
				""
				"Though they may seem insignificant compared to the greater horrors lurking deeper within the Hollows, Corrodents are fast, aggressive, and rarely travel alone. Underestimating them can quickly prove fatal."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"High above the cavern floor drift the mysterious &5Gloomoths&r, gentle creatures whose glowing wings provide one of the few natural sources of light within the darkness."
				""
				"Unlike most creatures, Gloomoths are naturally attracted to &elight sources&r and can often be seen circling torches, lanterns, and other glowing blocks. Unfortunately, this behavior also makes them easy prey for the &8Underzealots&r, who lure them into ancient rituals hidden throughout the Hollows."
				""
				"Defeating both Gloomoths and Underzealots rewards valuable materials used in advanced crafting recipes and prepares you for the darker mysteries that still await."
				""
				"Every creature has its place within the Hollows."
				""
				"Understanding them is often just as important as defeating them."
			]
